== Recent News

- \[April 2025\] We have released the [https://github.com/NVlabs/dexmimicgen/ DexMimicGen simulation environments and datasets] and the [https://github.com/NVlabs/AHA/ AHA codebase].

- \[April 2025\] 3 papers presented at ICLR 2025: [https://openreview.net/forum?id=LqhorpRLIm&referrer=%5BAuthor%20Console%5D(%2Fgroup%3Fid%3DICLR.cc%2F2025%2FConference%2FAuthors%23your-submissions) MimicLabs] (a study in collecting and using large-scale manipulation datasets), [https://aha-vlm.github.io/ AHA] (novel failure data generation and failure reasoning framework for robotic manipulation), and [https://latentactionpretraining.github.io/ LAPA] (unsupervised latent action based pretraining for robotic manipulation).

- \[March 2025\] Check out [https://co-training.github.io/ Sim-and-Real Co-Training], a simple recipe that utilizes synthetic data generation tools (such as [https://mimicgen.github.io/ MimicGen]) for efficient real-world robotic manipulation. This recipe was used to train the [https://developer.nvidia.com/isaac/gr00t GR00T-N1] humanoid foundation model as well.

== About Me

I am a research scientist at NVIDIA AI. I obtained my PhD degree from Stanford University, co-advised by [http://cvgl.stanford.edu/silvio/ Silvio Savarese] and [http://vision.stanford.edu/feifeili/ Fei-Fei Li]. My research focuses on developing systems and algorithms to enable robots to learn useful manipulation tasks.

